# Pre-Feature Selection Checkpoint

## Required Context
Before proceeding with feature selection, verify the following context elements:

1. Current state of core-mechanics.mdc
   - All feature statuses must be accurate
   - Previous feature should be marked as [done] if complete

2. Current state of active-working-feature-context.mdc
   - If a previous feature exists, it should be properly recorded
   - Previous feature status should match core-mechanics.mdc

## Verification Steps
- [ ] Run a scan of core-mechanics.mdc to identify all features and their statuses
- [ ] Compare with active-working-feature-context.mdc for consistency
- [ ] Resolve any inconsistencies before proceeding
- [ ] If transitioning from a previous feature, verify all its tests pass
- [ ] Ensure the implementation files for the previous feature are complete

## Context Restoration
If context has been lost or is incomplete:
1. Examine core-mechanics.mdc to identify the current feature set
2. Review the most recent implementation files to determine their status
3. Update active-working-feature-context.mdc to reflect the actual state
4. Document any discrepancies found in the restoration process

## Expected Output
After completing this checkpoint, you should have:
- Clear understanding of all feature statuses
- Accurate representation of the previous feature's state
- Consistent status indicators across all relevant files
- A solid foundation for selecting the next feature to implement 